WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:18.462
The morning Little Joe and Merrylegs left for the minister's house.

2
00:00:21.605 --> 00:00:24.948
Then John saddled Ginger and mounted, leading me beside her.

3
00:00:26.869 --> 00:00:29.892
We rode out through the gates of Birtwick Park without looking back.

4
00:00:32.272 --> 00:00:35.954
After about fifteen miles we came to a place called Earlshall Park.

5
00:00:36.394 --> 00:00:37.595
This would be our new home.

6
00:00:39.836 --> 00:00:42.578
The estate had a very fancy house and a large stable.

7
00:00:45.259 --> 00:00:47.981
When we reached the stableyard, John asked for Mr.

8
00:00:48.021 --> 00:00:53.744
York. York was the man in charge of the earl's stable, horses, and carriages.

9
00:00:55.765 --> 00:00:59.147
He was a handsome man with a manner that said he expected to be obeyed.

10
00:00:59.167 --> 00:01:02.648
"It's nice to meet you," he said to John.

11
00:01:02.668 --> 00:01:04.909
"Thanks for delivering the new horses."

12
00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:08.831
He called for the grooms to take Ginger and me inside.

13
00:01:10.052 --> 00:01:12.232
Then he invited John to come and have some tea.

14
00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:16.274
The grooms led us into the bright, airy stable.

15
00:01:19.275 --> 00:01:24.678
One led me into a large, deeply bedded stall, and the other took Ginger into the equally nice

16
00:01:24.698 --> 00:01:25.478
stall beside it.

17
00:01:27.679 --> 00:01:29.700
Then they groomed us and gave us some hay.

18
00:01:30.996 --> 00:01:32.657
Half an hour later John and Mr.

19
00:01:32.677 --> 00:01:33.378
York returned.

20
00:01:34.859 --> 00:01:36.260
York looked us over carefully.

21
00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:40.383
"These look like very nice horses, Mr.

22
00:01:40.423 --> 00:01:41.964
Manly," he said to John.

23
00:01:41.984 --> 00:01:45.107
"Is there anything you'd like to tell me about them?

24
00:01:45.787 --> 00:01:47.268
All horses have their quirks."

25
00:01:48.889 --> 00:01:52.412
"I don't believe there's a better pair of horses in the country," John replied.

26
00:01:52.432 --> 00:01:55.314
"I'm very sorry to part with them.

27
00:01:55.995 --> 00:01:57.736
But you should know that they're not alike.

28
00:01:58.804 --> 00:02:01.565
The black one has the most perfect nature I've ever seen.

29
00:02:02.606 --> 00:02:06.847
I don't think he's ever known a harsh word or an unfair punishment since he was foaled."

30
00:02:08.648 --> 00:02:10.249
"Excellent," York said.

31
00:02:10.269 --> 00:02:14.311
"But the chestnut one hasn't been so lucky," John went on.

32
00:02:14.331 --> 00:02:19.333
"We bought her from a dealer who said she'd had some bad treatment in her early years.

33
00:02:20.513 --> 00:02:22.894
When we got her, she was tense and suspicious.

34
00:02:23.955 --> 00:02:28.452
But after some good handling at our place, she relaxed, and for the past three years she's been

35
00:02:28.492 --> 00:02:28.993
very good."

36
00:02:30.093 --> 00:02:31.753
"I see," York said.

37
00:02:31.773 --> 00:02:36.215
"If she's well-treated, there isn't a better, more willing animal," John said.

38
00:02:36.235 --> 00:02:38.335
"But she's still high-strung.

39
00:02:39.315 --> 00:02:43.997
She's more bothered by flies than most horses, and likely to be annoyed by the harness too.

40
00:02:45.097 --> 00:02:48.218
If she were unfairly treated, she'd probably react strongly."

41
00:02:49.838 --> 00:02:53.239
"Many spirited horses are like that," York said with a nod.

42
00:02:53.259 --> 00:02:55.460
"Thank you for the information, Mr.

43
00:02:56.768 --> 00:02:58.410
Manly. I'll remember what you've told me."

44
00:02:58.430 --> 00:03:02.313
"Oh, I almost forgot to mention one more thing," John said.

45
00:03:02.333 --> 00:03:06.677
"We've never used the checkrein to hold up the head of either of these horses.

46
00:03:08.018 --> 00:03:12.162
The black horse has never worn one in his life, and the dealer said it's what spoiled the

47
00:03:12.182 --> 00:03:17.387
mare." "Well, they're going to have to wear it here, I'm afraid," York said.

48
00:03:17.407 --> 00:03:22.432
"I prefer a loose rein myself, and the earl doesn't care.

49
00:03:23.284 --> 00:03:26.927
But the lady is very interested in style and fashion.

50
00:03:28.148 --> 00:03:32.411
If her carriage horses aren't reined up tight, she won't even look at them."

51
00:03:32.431 --> 00:03:36.453
"I'm sorry to hear that," John said with a sigh.

52
00:03:36.473 --> 00:03:39.356
"But I'd better go, or I'll miss my train."

53
00:03:40.656 --> 00:03:42.117
John stepped into my stall.

54
00:03:42.138 --> 00:03:46.541
"Good-bye, you two," he said, giving Ginger and me each a pat.

55
00:03:47.241 --> 00:03:48.242
"I hope you'll be happy here."

56
00:03:49.763 --> 00:03:50.964
His voice sounded sad.

57
00:03:51.676 --> 00:03:54.798
All I could do to say good-bye was hold my face close to him.

58
00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:59.742
Soon he was gone, and to this day I've never seen him since.

59
00:04:02.944 --> 00:04:04.885
The next day the earl came to look at us.

60
00:04:05.866 --> 00:04:07.467
He seemed pleased by what he saw.

61
00:04:07.487 --> 00:04:12.230
"These horses are just as nice as squire said," he commented.

62
00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:17.914
"It's too bad they're not a match in color, but they'll be fine for driving around the countryside."

63
00:04:19.315 --> 00:04:19.916
York agreed.

64
00:04:20.532 --> 00:04:22.793
Then he told the earl what John had said about us.

65
00:04:22.813 --> 00:04:26.275
"Hmm." The earl glanced at Ginger.

66
00:04:26.295 --> 00:04:30.256
"Keep an eye on the mare, and start with the checkrein loose.

67
00:04:31.557 --> 00:04:35.259
If you tighten it up a little at a time, I'm sure they'll both get used to it

68
00:04:35.319 --> 00:04:37.560
soon. I'll mention it to my wife."

69
00:04:39.741 --> 00:04:42.402
That afternoon the grooms harnessed us to a fine carriage.

70
00:04:43.963 --> 00:04:46.724
For the first time I had the checkrein attached to my bridle.

71
00:04:47.688 --> 00:04:50.449
It was strange not to be able to lower my head if I wished.

72
00:04:51.469 --> 00:04:55.210
But my head wasn't held any higher than normal, so I didn't mind too much.

73
00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:57.131
Ginger didn't complain either.

74
00:04:58.691 --> 00:05:02.012
As the clock struck three, we were led around to the front of the house.

75
00:05:04.833 --> 00:05:08.734
With a rustling of silk, a proud-looking lady walked down the steps to meet us.

76
00:05:10.314 --> 00:05:12.075
She looked at Ginger and me and frowned.

77
00:05:12.715 --> 00:05:15.416
But she said nothing—at least not on that first day.
